// Second player-authored RapidRanged spell, following eldritch_blast.ron's
// now-reviewed shape in this same folder: same variant, same fire_all
// burst pattern, scaled up for a 1st-circle spell (3 darts instead of 2,
// higher per-dart damage and energy cost). See eldritch_blast.ron's own
// header for the full reasoning on why RapidRanged fires every projectile
// along the same look direction (no independent per-dart aim exists in
// common/src/states/rapid_ranged.rs) -- in practice all 3 darts land on
// the SAME target, not spread across "nearby foes" the way the sheet's own
// flavor implies; the i18n description below is written to avoid promising
// a multi-target spread this engine can't deliver. The "unerringly"
// auto-hit framing is not modeled either: RapidRanged has no auto_aim
// field (unlike BasicRanged, which does), so this resolves as a normal
// to-hit ranged attack roll per dart, same as every other ranged spell.
RapidRanged(
    energy_cost: 10,
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    shoot_duration: 0.05,
    recover_duration: 0.35,
    options: (
        max_projectiles: Some(3),
        fire_all: true,
    ),
    projectile: (
        kind: Simple,
        attack: Some((
            damage: 6,
            damage_kind: Force,
        )),
    ),
    projectile_body: Object(BoltFire),
    projectile_speed: 80.0,
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
